    "q-109079": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109079",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "The probability distribution of the random variable $X$ is given below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{9}{2},$ calculate $\\text{Var}[3-\\frac{1}{2}X].$ \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that for any random variable $X$ and constants $a$ and $b,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[aX+b]={a}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $b=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3-\\frac{1}{2}X] & ={(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can compute the variance of $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nAdditionally, we're given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{9}{2}.$ \n\nWe start by computing $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={0}^{2}\\cdot f(0)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+36\\cdot \\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{99}{4}-{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[3-\\frac{1}{2}X] & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\text{Var}[X] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-109079-a",
